  "site_name": "Moore House, Flat 9",
  "epc_number": "0158-3885-7333-9603-9175",
  "pp_id": "14496883",
  "subdivision_of_building": "The proposal only affects Flat 9 (top floor) of Moore House",
  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Change of use of an existing self-contained residential flat (Use Class C3) to short-term letting / temporary sleeping accommodation for up to 365 days per year. No physical alterations are proposed to the flat or to the building.\n\nI have lived in London for 11 years, and for the last 7 years this flat has been my main home. Due to important family reasons, I now need to spend extended periods in Italy. However, London remains a central part of my personal and professional life. I return regularly for work, business meetings, studies, and also to see close friends and family. For this reason, I will continue using the flat personally for several months each year. When I am away, I would like to rent the property on a short-term basis to help cover the significant costs of maintaining the flat, while fully preserving its residential use for when I am in London.\n\nThe intention is to host mainly families and responsible visitors who wish to stay in Hackney, an area known for its parks, community atmosphere and excellent connections. This is a small-scale, carefully managed operation designed for quiet guests who respect the building and the neighbourhood. The flat accommodates a maximum of 3 people and is operated with strict house rules, supervised check-ins, and clear expectations to ensure that guests behave respectfully at all times.\n\nI have always had an excellent relationship with my neighbours and with the building community. I value this relationship deeply and would never undertake any activity that could cause disturbance or inconvenience. My priority is to maintain a peaceful and well-managed environment, fully respecting the residential character of Moore House. I remain committed to addressing any concerns promptly and ensuring that the proposed use is carried out responsibly, safely and with full consideration for those living around me.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in the effective loss of a permanent residential unit (Class C3), reducing the borough’s long-term housing supply. The proposal fails to demonstrate that continued C3 use is unviable and would undermine Hackney’s ability to meet identified housing needs. The development is therefore contrary to policies H8 (Loss of existing housing and estate redevelopment) and H9 (Ensuring the best use of stock) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP12 (Housing Supply), LP24 (Loss of Housing), and LP25 (Visitor Accommodation) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (LP33).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in increased noise and disturbance associated with frequent guest turnover and servicing activity. This would be detrimental to the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers and harmful to the established residential character of the building. The proposal is contrary to policy D14 (Noise) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP2 (Development and Amenity) and LP58 (Managing Impacts of Development) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (LP33) (2020).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
